## 2. Generate synthetic data

PAR is trained once and `m_syn` synthetic datasets are drawn from it.   <!-- PAR -->
Sections 3-8 and 10 look at dataset 1; section 9b pools the PART 4 results over all `m_syn` datasets.
**DATA CHANGES (generator input only):** `participant_id` is passed as text; `on_any_steroid` is modelled as a category
(0/1). Values are not changed.   <!-- PAR -->

```{r generate}
# ---- Generate m_syn datasets with PAR ----   # PAR: replaces the VAE call
corsano_syn_list <- generate_synthetic_par(corsano_real,
                                           id_var = "participant_id",
                                           time_var = "Days_since_bio",
                                           context_vars = traits,                 # resp class, sex, age, BMI
                                           categorical_vars = "on_any_steroid",
                                           epochs = 128,
                                           seed = seed_to_assess,
                                           m = m_syn)

