## 9b. Model transfer, pooled over the m synthetic datasets

Same idea as synthpop's `summary.fit.synds()` / `compare.fit.synds()` (Raab, Nowok & Dibben 2016): fit the PART 4 model
to each of the m synthetic datasets, average the estimates, and combine the standard errors.
For each estimate (bi-weekly mean, Non-Responder - Responder, change from day 0, covariate):

* est_syn = q̄ = mean of the m estimates
* se_syn = √(v̄ (1 + 1/m)), v̄ = mean of the m squared SEs (complete synthesis, model trained once, synthetic n = real n)
* z_diff = (q̄ − real estimate) / √(real SE² / m): how far the pooled estimate is from the real one.
  If the synthetic data were right, z_diff ~ N(0, 1), so the mean |z_diff| would be about √(2/π) = 0.80

Knots can differ between datasets; that does not matter here, because means, contrasts and covariate effects are on the
data's scale whatever the spline basis.

```{r knots per dataset}
# knots BIC picked: real, and each synthetic dataset
knots_all <- map_dfr(key_vars, function(v) {
  tibble(variable = v,
         knots_real = best_knots(real_fits[[v]]),
         knots_syn = paste(map_chr(syn_fits_list, ~ if (is.null(.x[[v]])) "NA" else as.character(best_knots(.x[[v]]))),
                           collapse = ", "))
})
print(as.data.frame(knots_all))
```

